{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48447", "qid": "gen-paper-b2cdb955", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "How many observables does analysis 2408.03744 measure?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2408.03744 measures 24 distinct observables, including double ratios, fiducial and total cross sections, and ratios of cross sections between different energies for W and Z bosons. Here are the observables:\n\n- Double ratio: fiducial (W+/W-) ratio at 13 TeV over 5.02 TeV\n- Double ratio: fiducial (W/Z) ratio at 13 TeV over 5.02 TeV\n- Double ratio: total (W+/W-) ratio at 13 TeV over 5.02 TeV\n- Double ratio: total (W/Z) ratio at 13 TeV over 5.02 TeV\n- Fiducial cross section ratio W+/W-\n- Fiducial cross section ratio W/Z\n- Fiducial inclusive cross section times branching fraction, W+ -> l+ nu\n- Fiducial inclusive cross section times branching fraction, W- -> l- nubar\n- Fiducial inclusive cross section times branching fraction, Z -> l+l- (60-120 GeV)\n- Fiducial inclusive cross section times branching fraction, inclusive W -> l nu\n- Ratio of fiducial W+ cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of fiducial W- cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of fiducial Z cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of fiducial inclusive W cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of total W+ cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of total W- cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of total Z cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Ratio of total inclusive W cross section between 13 and 5.02 TeV\n- Total cross section ratio W+/W-\n- Total cross section ratio W/Z\n- Total inclusive cross section times branching fraction, W+ -> l+ nu\n- Total inclusive cross section times branching fraction, W- -> l- nubar\n- Total inclusive cross section times branching fraction, Z -> l+l- (60-120 GeV)\n- Total inclusive cross section times branching fraction, inclusive W -> l nu\n\nThis list is based on the direct assertions in the graph. \n\nAnswer: Analysis 2408.03744 measures 24 distinct observables.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2408.03744 measures 24 distinct observables, including double ratios, fiducial and total cross sections, and ratios of cross sections between different energies for W and Z bosons.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 24, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:fid_dblratio_wpm", "hepkg:observable:fid_dblratio_wz", "hepkg:observable:fid_enratio_w", "hepkg:observable:fid_enratio_wminus", "hepkg:observable:fid_enratio_wplus", "hepkg:observable:fid_enratio_z", "hepkg:observable:fid_ratio_wpm", "hepkg:observable:fid_ratio_wz", "hepkg:observable:fid_xsec_w", "hepkg:observable:fid_xsec_wminus", "hepkg:observable:fid_xsec_wplus", "hepkg:observable:fid_xsec_z", "hepkg:observable:tot_dblratio_wpm", "hepkg:observable:tot_dblratio_wz", "hepkg:observable:tot_enratio_w", "hepkg:observable:tot_enratio_wminus", "hepkg:observable:tot_enratio_wplus", "hepkg:observable:tot_enratio_z", "hepkg:observable:tot_ratio_wpm", "hepkg:observable:tot_ratio_wz", "hepkg:observable:tot_xsec_w", "hepkg:observable:tot_xsec_wminus", "hepkg:observable:tot_xsec_wplus", "hepkg:observable:tot_xsec_z"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0824895f60bf689938ffa556", "hepkg:evidence:315f85d1ae066a15209d2b75", "hepkg:evidence:367b182335c17cc9b453eec4", "hepkg:evidence:3f65d54dfebf57680e49839d", "hepkg:evidence:78b57620260b2b0c9087ba3f", "hepkg:evidence:841c43daa363dba929850145", "hepkg:evidence:a57e504d3d7550515009b4b7", "hepkg:evidence:abc77b204ec066184e663b8f", "