{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48447", "qid": "gen-paper-b538a62b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "How many detector objects does analysis 2309.14442 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2309.14442 defines 16 detector objects:\n\n- Additional b jet, particle level (b jet not originating from top quark decay)\n- Jet, detector level (anti-kT R=0.4, PF)\n- Jet, particle level (anti-kT R=0.4, excluding neutrinos)\n- Light jet, particle level (not matched to b hadron)\n- Light-tagged jet, detector level (fails DeepJet medium WP)\n- Particle-level (dressed) electron\n- Particle-level (dressed) muon\n- Primary (signal) electron, detector level\n- Primary (signal) muon, detector level\n- Veto electron, detector level\n- Veto electron, particle level\n- Veto muon, detector level\n- Veto muon, particle level\n- b jet, particle level (matched to b hadron)\n- b-tagged jet, detector level, DeepJet medium working point\n- b-tagged jet, detector level, DeepJet tight working point\n\nThese objects are a mix of detector-level and particle-level definitions, covering jets, leptons, and b-jets with various working points and selections.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2309.14442 defines 16 detector objects, including jets, leptons, and b-jets with various working points and selections.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2303.15340", "2309.14442", "2402.08486"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2309.14442"], "predicate": "result_defines_object"}, "rows": 16, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:object:additional_bjet_particle", "hepkg:object:bjet_medium_detector", "hepkg:object:bjet_particle", "hepkg:object:bjet_tight_detector", "h