{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48447", "qid": "gen-paper-b58acad3", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2404.06204 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2404.06204 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Best Linear Unbiased Estimator (BLUE) combination of electron and muon channel measurements\n- Bootstrap method to estimate statistical correlation between \\( p_T^{ll} \\) and \\( u_T \\)-based Z measurements\n- Iterative Bayesian (D'Agostini) unfolding method\n- Pseudo-experiment (toy) variations of data and MC samples to estimate statistical uncertainties\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as the statistical methods used by the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2404.06204"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2404.06204"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.035}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:statmethod:blue-combination", "hepkg:statmethod:bootstrap-correlation-estimation", "hepkg:statmethod:iterative-bayesian-unfolding", "hepkg:statmethod:pseudo-experiment-toy-variation"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:139bca98197116c96718fef8", "hepkg:evidence:6cf1524f3d662964024fc355", "hepkg:evidence:aa762dd14fd90294070a41e4", "hepkg:evidence:afc6b1332d4417463dc0ac40"], "seen_values": ["2404.06204", "agostini", "and", "bayesian", "best", "between", "blue", "bootstrap", "channel", "combination", "correlation", "data", "electron", "estimate", "estimator", "hepkg:statmethod:blue-combination", "hepkg:statmethod:bootstrap-correlation-estimation", "hepkg:statmethod:iterative-bayesian-unfolding", "hepkg:statmethod:pseudo-experiment-toy-variation", "iterative", "linear", "ll-", "measurements", "method", "muon", "p_t", "pseudo-experiment", "result_uses_statis