{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48447", "qid": "gen-paper-b742dd52", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2209.07327 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2209.07327 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Charge misidentification background uncertainty\n- DeepAK8 heavy-particle tagging and misidentification uncertainty\n- DeepAK8 light quark/gluon score correction uncertainty\n- DeepJet b tagging efficiency/misidentification uncertainty\n- Dilepton (ee, e-mu, mu-mu) trigger scale factor uncertainty\n- Electron identification scale factor uncertainty\n- Electron reconstruction and isolation scale factor uncertainty\n- H_T distribution correction uncertainty for W+jets background\n- H_T distribution correction uncertainty for ttbar background\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) and jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- L1 ECAL trigger timing correction uncertainty\n- Multilepton channel muon nonprompt-rate eta-dependence uncertainty\n- Multilepton channel nonprompt background normalization uncertainty by lepton flavor category\n- Multilepton channel nonprompt-rate uncertainty (electron/muon)\n- Multilepton channel prompt-rate uncertainty\n- Muon identification and isolation scale factor uncertainty\n- Parton distribution function (PDF) uncertainty\n- Pileup modeling uncertainty\n- Renormalization and factorization scale uncertainty\n- SS dilepton channel nonprompt-rate uncertainty\n- SS dilepton channel prompt-rate uncertainty\n- Single-lepton trigger scale factor uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis 2209.07327.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676